e coverage thresholds in CI.",\n          "fix": "Add to requirements-dev.txt: pytest-cov && run: pytest --cov=. tests/ && add coverage threshold to CI"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "ci_hardening": {\n      "score": 6,\n      "max": 20,\n      "findings": [\n        {\n          "id": "CI-001",\n          "severity": "HIGH",\n          "title": "No CI/CD workflow file found",\n          "file": ".github/workflows/",\n          "line": null,\n          "evidence": "No .github/workflows/*.yml files found in project structure. No GitHub Actions workflow defined.",\n          "description": "Without CI/CD, code quality, security, and test checks are not automated. Deployments are manual and error-prone.",\n          "fix": "Create .github/workflows/ci.yml with: linting (flake8/ruff), testing (pytest), security scanning (bandit), and deployment steps"\n        },\n        {\n          "id": "CI-002",\n          "severity": "HIGH",\n          "title": "LICENSE file not found in audit scope",\n          "file": "LICENSE",\n          "line": null,\n          "evidence": "README states \'MIT License — See the LICENSE file for details\' but LICENSE file content not provided in audit.",\n          "description": "For a public/distributed project, a LICENSE file is critical. Without it, legal status is unclear and enterprise adoption is blocked.",\n          "fix": "Create LICENSE file with MIT license text: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"\n        },\n        {\n          "id": "CI-003",\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "title": "No SECURITY.md vulnerability disclosure policy",\n          "file": "SECURITY.md",\n          "line": null,\n          "evidence": "No SECURITY.md file found in project structure.",\n          "description": "Enterprise adopters expect a published vulnerability disclosure policy. Without it, security researchers have no clear path to report issues.",\n          "fix": "Create SECURITY.md with: contact email, SLA (Critical: 7 days, 